# build/game-cpp-dc.hxml — the recompiled game through reflaxe.CPP, for the Dreamcast.
#
# build/game-cpp.hxml with fastmem (ADR-0049): guest RAM and the scratchpad reached through the
# SH-4's MMU, one masked load or store an access, everything else a TLB miss the backend emulates.
# A tree transpiled this way is the Dreamcast's alone — its accesses are SH-4 assembly — and
# scripts/build-dc.sh sees it (mem_Fastmem.cpp) and builds it with RECOMPSX_FASTMEM; a desktop
# build of it stops at mem.Fastmem's #error. Transpile with build/game-cpp.hxml for the desktop.
build/game-cpp.hxml
-D recompsx_fastmem
